lazar (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Representative María Elvira Salazar seeks another term in a Miami-area district that leans Republican by about six points. She faces Democrat Eliott Rodriguez, a well-funded challenger who raised $1.3 million and kept the race close in recent polling, including a tie and a one-point Republican lead in surveys sponsored by Democratic groups. Salazar, however, holds a decisive financial advantage, with $2 million on hand and far greater spending capacity.\n\nEvery major expert rating, from Cook to the Silver Bulletin, places the race in the Lean or Likely Republican column, and prediction markets give Salazar roughly a two-thirds chance. Democratic leader Hakeem Jeffries has campaigned with Rodriguez, and a controversy over a Cuban bakery event has drawn attention, but the structural fundamentals still favor the incumbent in this competitive but Republican-leaning seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2129, "margin": -4.43}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2851, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2818, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3773, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2766, "margin": -3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3218, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3331, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3785, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3582, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3814, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3691, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3705, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3683, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.315, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3051, "margin": -2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3209, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3463, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.324, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.3188, "